<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hastings</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1066">1066</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norman-conquest">Norman Conquest</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hastings was fought on 14 October 1066 near Hastings in Sussex, where Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William of Normandy</a> defeated and killed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harold-godwinson">Harold Godwinson</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. The victory began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norman-conquest">Norman Conquest</a>: William was crowned king on Christmas Day 1066, and a new Norman aristocracy replaced the English nobility.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hastings.jpg" alt="Battle of Hastings" width="320" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Myrabella · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bayeux_Tapestry_scene57_Harold_death.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
